msm: a stream refill uploads the half it just read, on MPT_PC
Applied in order by runtimes/gc_wii/mp4/CMakeLists.txt with `git apply`.

msmStreamData reads the next half of a stream's ring with DVDReadAsync and toggles bufNo after the call.
msmStreamDvdCallback then uploads the half that bufNo names, which assumes the read completes after the
toggle, as it always does on the console. The PC DVD layer can complete the read and run the callback
inside DVDReadAsync, before the toggle, so every upload went to the other half: one half late. While a
stream plays, the late upload still lands just before the voice reaches that half. At the end of a
non-looping stream no later read uploads the last half, so the voice played that half's contents from
two halves earlier. Every minigame's winner or draw jingle (streams 1 and 4) ended with 0.58 s of
audio from 2.0 s before instead of its real ending. On PC, bufNo is toggled before the read is issued.
Changes what msm uploads to the stream ring, so state hashes move (docs/titles/mp4.md section 15).

diff --git a/src/msm/msmstream.c b/src/msm/msmstream.c
index c2f0998..1e9e1ec 100644
--- a/src/msm/msmstream.c
+++ b/src/msm/msmstream.c
@@ -806,7 +806,18 @@ static void msmStreamData(s32 streamNo) {
             }
             slot->streamPos += readSize;
             slot->readBusyF = 1;
+#ifdef MPT_PC
+            /* The read may complete, and msmStreamDvdCallback run, before DVDReadAsync returns. The
+             * callback uploads the half that bufNo names after the toggle below, as on the console,
+             * where the read always completes later. Toggle first, so the half just read is the one
+             * uploaded. Otherwise each upload lags a half behind, and a stream's last half, which no
+             * later read uploads, plays the ring's stale contents from two halves earlier. */
+            slot->bufNo ^= 1;
+            DVDReadAsync(&slot->file, dataPtr, readSize, slot->streamBaseOfs + (slot->streamPos - readSize), msmStreamDvdCallback);
+            return;
+#else
             DVDReadAsync(&slot->file, dataPtr, readSize, slot->streamBaseOfs + (slot->streamPos - readSize), msmStreamDvdCallback);
+#endif
         }
     } else if (slot->firstF != 0) {
         slot->firstF= 0;
